IMPLEMENTATION SUMMARY (SwiftUI + Apple HIG, ADR-002/005/006/011/013/014/015)
  - SwiftUI `View` + `@Observable SettingsPageModel` (ADR-004 seam pattern); no networking/business logic in the view body.
  - Adaptive: centered readable column on macOS/iPad (max 720pt), full width on iPhone; cards restack at
    accessibility Dynamic Type sizes (SettingsActionCard switches H→V on `dynamicTypeSize.isAccessibilitySize`).
  - Data source `useSettings → GET /settings` ported as `SettingsPageSource` (in-memory double + AppSettingsPageSource
    production adapter). 3 web card actions ported faithfully: `<a href="/data-export">`, `dispatchTourLauncherOpen()`
    (→ Notification.Name.teslaSyncTourLauncherRequested), `restartChecklist()` (→ resets the two UserDefaults flags
    teslasync:checklist:{dismissed,completed-at}, exactly as the web setChecklistDismissed(false)+setChecklistCompletedAt(null)).
  - EditConflictBanner ported via SettingsEditLease seam (web useEditLease) with "Take over editing" → claim().
  - 4 data states for the source: loading (ProgressView/TSPageLoader), success (content), empty (ContentUnavailableView),
    error (error view + Retry) — never a blank region.
  - Tokens-only styling (P2): TSGlassPanel/TSIconBox/TSButton/TSAlertBanner/TSPageLoader/TSEmptyState/typography; materials
    where the web uses glass (ADR-005). a11y: header traits, button traits/hints, VoiceOver labels, ≥44pt targets,
    Dynamic Type, light/dark/increased-contrast via the generated dynamic-color tokens (ADR-015).
  - i18n: every visible string via LocalizedStringKey resolved from Localizable.xcstrings; web key names kept verbatim (ADR-014).

